cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  SARGuardian: measured limits of NISAR L-band SAR for
  Himalayan slope-failure early warning
message: >-
  If you use this software or its results, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Sarker
    given-names: Moshiour Rahman
repository-code: https://github.com/moshiour0/SARGuardian
abstract: >-
  A pipeline and measurement campaign testing what NISAR Level-2
  products can and cannot see of a Himalayan slope failure. Over the
  confirmed source zone of the 26 August 2026 Langtang massif collapse,
  offset tracking on the one geometry with a stable detection floor
  shows no displacement above 18.6 mm/day in the seven weeks before
  failure, with the last observation seven days out. The interferometric
  product retains 0-3% of its pixels over this terrain and cannot
  address it at all. The failure itself is detectable only as loss of
  correlation, at 14-35 times the event-free baseline on both
  geometries. Four measured limits, and the revisit and product-type
  requirements that follow from them.
keywords:
  - InSAR
  - NISAR
  - synthetic aperture radar
  - offset tracking
  - landslide
  - early warning
  - Himalaya
license: MIT
